F][/dim]the command keeps running as a live, first-class monitor member of [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]their agent family — with streaming output, live runtime, custom [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]start/stop statuses, a timeout, and an optional follow-up agent [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]that resumes the same workspace and conversation when the command [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]finishes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]12[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]sase_monitor.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/sase_monitor.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-kp[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-kp/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Monitor marker fields on the agent scan wire[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-wire[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-wire: add the monitor marker fields to the Rust `AgentMetaWire` / [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`DoneMarkerWire` and their Python mirrors so monitor members survive the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent artifact scan.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]First-class custom agent status labels[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]status-bucket[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]status-bucket: give `Agent` an explicit status-bucket override and route[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agent-shaped bucket lookups through one accessor so arbitrary status [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]labels bucket correctly.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Monitor member lifecycle and supervisor process[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]engine-run[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-wire, status-bucket[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]engine-run: create the monitor family member, run and stream the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]monitored command from a detached supervisor, enforce the timeout, own [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the workspace claim, and write the terminal marker.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Follow-up agent handoff after a monitor completes[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]engine-next[dim] · [dim][/dim]after engine-run[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]engine-next: compose the command breakdown, resume the starter's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]conversation with `#fork`, and launch the follow-up agent into the same [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lane and workspace.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]In-agent handoff marker and runner adoption[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]handoff[dim] · [dim][/dim]after engine-run[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]handoff: add the `.sase_monitor_pending` handoff so `sase monitor start`[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]kills the calling agent cleanly, saves its chat for `#fork`, and never [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]releases the workspace.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase monitor command group[/bold #D7AFFF]                                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli[dim] · [dim][/dim]after engine-next, handoff[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli: add `sase monitor start|stop|list|show` with multi-format output, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]duration parsing, and monitor id resolution.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Monitor rows in agent lists and family rosters[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]tui-rows[dim] · [dim][/dim]after status-bucket, engine-run[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui-rows: render monitor members in the Agents tab, family roster, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]integration agent lists with their own glyph, phase label, live runtime,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and status.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Monitor detail panel, live output, and keybindings[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]tui-detail[dim] · [dim][/dim]after tui-rows, cli[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui-detail: render the monitor detail section and live command output, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and wire the stop action into the footer and help modal.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Approved-epic launch runs as a monitor[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]epic-launch[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]epic-launch: replace the detached epic-launch task with a generic [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]monitor start using `EPIC APPROVED` / `EPIC CREATED`, keeping the host [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]claim and a fallback.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]/sase_monitor skill[/bold #D7AFFF]                                          [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]skill[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]skill: author the `/sase_monitor` skill source so agents prefer it over [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]their own monitor and scheduled wake-up tools.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Memory and documentation updates[/bold #D7AFFF]                             [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]memory-docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after skill[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]memory-docs: update the build-and-run memory note, regenerate agent [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]instruction files, and document monitors.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  12 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]End-to-end monitor exercises[/bold #D7AFFF]                                 [bold black on #5FD7AF] xsmall [/bold black on #5FD7AF]\n    [#AF87FF]smoke[dim] · [dim][/dim]after tui-detail, epic-launch, memory-docs[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]smoke: launch real agents that exercise the sleep, timeout, stop, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]follow-up monitor paths and report what the surfaces actually showed.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-kp","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-kp.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-85349858cd7b13f02d92bd7cbd5ed7fb","started_at":"2026-08-12T21:34:29.764667+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1786576908,"sha":"b32167c31bca2e28d6dfbd6e8cd5dd86a07a883f","subject":"feat(monitor): add monitor member lifecycle and supervisor process"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"81231f2ba50a2368838b0f83807f77818096563c0913b5b44c035186066816a5","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-kp.3/chat.md","size_bytes":9690},"commits":{"digest":"a305cf0684771f57684e1d81e01b80b09c06abc0d9238ce179e2962d64dbfa04","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-kp.3/commits.json","size_bytes":244},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-kp.3/e